{"post": true, "caption": "Most traders pick the size first, then squeeze the stop to fit. That's backwards.\nDecide your risk (say 1% of the account), place the stop where the setup is proven wrong, then let the math pick the size.\nPosition size = risk amount / stop distance. Wider stop, smaller size. Same pain if wrong.\n\nEducation only. Not financial advice.\n\n#CandleAndCode #TraderMath #PositionSizing #RiskManagement #TradingPH", "tag": "// trader math", "footer": "Education only. Not financial advice.", "bpm": 92, "scenes": [
